+# Revision 1 delta
+
+The original script candidate receipt is `18f8b40a7718ef958edad7ef67dad8bbe919732ec1572c9a600e8cf4a7ed29d4`. That frozen directory is unchanged. This revision also preserves its receipt and all 31 listed artifacts in `evidence/previous-candidate/`, including the earlier failed audit-harness attempt. All six installable consumer/test/document candidates and the original source plan, candidate patch, audit and consumer test evidence retain their original bytes.
+
+The first change makes the committed migration checkpoint contain a resolvable script receipt closure. Installation copies the current frozen `receipt.json` and every listed artifact, preserving relative paths under `evidence/integration-scripts/`. Every copied file is checked against its pinned hash and source hash; the copied package is checked again as a whole before source installation or plain-queue removal. Subsequent stages reverify this checkpoint copy. No dependency tree is copied; the preserved scripts and history are small text artifacts.
+
+The second change rejects a resolved run output equal to or below the repository before any Git query, subprocess or output creation. This also excludes the checkpoint and symlink aliases into the repository. Later stages recheck the stored run directory. This prevents the supposedly read-only planning phase from creating its own dirty worktree.
+
+The PLAN now states the required storage checks without requiring an unrelated repeat of all Lean targets, the full bench test suite or global runner. The existing 14 focused storage tests, producer check, exact baseline/post-scope equality, queue/ledger equality, snapshot pins and size bound remain required. CI configuration is unchanged. Broader checks are recorded only if actually run. The script's result wording likewise records broader gates as not run rather than instructing an automatic full rerun.
+
+The optional reuse of a prior validation was deliberately not implemented. The plan still runs fresh baseline queue/scope checks against the explicit clean commit. There is no unchecked shortcut around a run's provenance or checked-input closure.
+
+The revision audit verifies both the original frozen package and its local historical copy, all six current source candidates, live preimages, unchanged consumer/policy pins, exact allowed integration function changes and unchanged remaining AST. The current test command runs 16 integration tests: eight unchanged utility tests and eight new tests for external output paths, symlink aliases, fail-before-side-effects ordering, complete relative artifact copies, source/archive corruption, missing files, path traversal and a tiny install-stage replay. The 14 unchanged consumer tests are inherited from the original receipt, not reported as a new execution. Two failed revision audit attempts are retained with script snapshots: the inserted test block initially changed indentation in the preceding original test; the AST audit detected the error before any integration test ran. Restoring both lines made the original class AST identical again. A separate patch-format rejection made no file changes. No live plan, migration, Lean/GPU work, proof change, primary-gate change, Git operation or repository write occurs here. Acceptance increment is zero.
